WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Threshold: the Decision Engine. An agent proposes; independent server policy determines execute, ask, defer, escalate or refuse.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A $35 refund passes verified evidence and delegated limits. Execution is a separate click; the synthetic action gets a persistent receipt.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Missing ownership produces Ask. Confidence cannot replace a required fact, and the original decision grants no execution authority.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
A synthetic resolver fills the missing fact and advances the evidence version. A new evaluation now permits execution; known failures are preserved.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Production exceeds staging authority. Escalate routes the exact proposal to an operator instead of expanding the agent’s scope.

6
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:04.000
A scoped sandbox reviewer records a reason. Approval binds the exact action, evidence version, policy and expiry; it can be revoked. Personas are synthetic.

7
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Failure test: CI changes after approval. Execution rechecks current evidence and refuses the deployment. No sandbox write is applied.

8
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:26.000
The audit records inputs, evidence, policy checks, reviews and receipts. Hash chaining detects inconsistency; external authenticity needs a signed anchor.

9
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Synthetic effects. Public policy demo. DeepSeek inference remains local.
